-- title:
--   Occurring calibrated weights satisfy every rank-two calibration condition
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a finite reduced irreducible crystallographic root system of positive rank, with a fixed positive system and simple roots $\alpha_i$, Weyl group $W$, and full weight lattice $P$. Fix $q\in\mathbb C^\times$ which is not a root of unity. Write $\widetilde H$ for its affine Hecke algebra with $T_i^2=(q-q^{-1})T_i+1$ and the Bernstein relation with denominator $1-X^{-\alpha_i}$ interpreted as a Laurent-polynomial divided difference. Let $T=\operatorname{Hom}(P,\mathbb C^\times)$, with $(wt)(X^\lambda)=t(X^{w^{-1}\lambda})$. All modules below are finite dimensional complex left modules. Irreducible modules are nonzero.
--
--   Let $M$ be calibrated and $t\in T$ satisfy $M_t\ne0$. For each pair of distinct simple roots $\alpha_i,\alpha_j$, let $R_{ij}$ be their generated rank-two root subsystem and $W_{ij}=\langle s_i,s_j\rangle$. Then
--   $$t\text{ is calibratable for every }R_{ij}.$$
--   Specifically, either $t(X^\alpha)\ne1$ for every $\alpha\in R_{ij}$, or $R_{ij}$ has type $C_2$ or $G_2$ and, labelling its long and short simple roots $\alpha_\ell,\alpha_s$, there is $u\in W_{ij}$ with $(ut)(X^{\alpha_\ell})=q^2$ and $(ut)(X^{\alpha_s})=1$, while $t(X^{\alpha_i})\ne1$ and $t(X^{\alpha_j})\ne1$.
--
--   Irreducibility is not required. This condition identifies the rank-two restrictions allowed for weights of calibrated modules.
-- source:
--   Calibrated representations of affine Hecke algebras, arXiv:math/0401323v2, PDF p. 18, Proposition 4.4

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Intake100_P26

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P26

open scoped BigOperators

variable {D : Datum} {V U : Type*}

variable [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℂ V] [AddCommGroup U] [Module ℂ U]

/-- Proposition 4.4, PDF p.18. Calibration suffices; irreducibility is not
assumed. Rank-two subsystems are generated by distinct simple roots. -/
theorem occurringWeightsCalibratable (D : Datum) (q : ℂ) (hq : GoodParameter q)
    (A : HeckeGenerators D V) [FiniteDimensional ℂ V] (hA : Relations q A)
    (hcal : Calibrated A) (t : Torus D) (ht : weightSpace A t ≠ ⊥) :
    ∀ i j : Fin D.rank, i ≠ j → Calibratable D q t i j := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Intake100.P26

end
